GUJ NEFT OUTAWARD DOUBT

GUJ.NEFT.OUT.COPY queue is used as a safety backup checkpoint —
MQOutput puts a message copy before main processing,
MQGet deletes it at the end if everything succeeds,
otherwise, it remains for reprocessing.

Soch jaise:

Tu ek bank transaction kar raha hai.

Pehle bank ek backup slip likh ke side me rakhta hai.

Agar transaction success ho gaya → slip phaad di (delete).

Agar failure aaya → slip se wapas transaction retry karega.

unit of work (UOW) ke andar aate hain.

> 👉 UOW = Either sab success (commit) ya sab fail (rollback).
Jab tak commit nahi hota — message “temporary” hota hai.
Commit hone ke baad agar success hua toh MQGet delete kar deta hai.
Agar exception hua toh rollback hone ke baad woh message reprocess queue ke liye available hota hai.

Main flow rollback hone ke baad IIB ek naya transaction kholta hai jisme exception flow COPY queue me message daal ke commit karta hai —
isliye reprocess flow ko message dikhta hai.”



So reprocess tabhi trigger hota hai jab:

1. Main transaction failed (rollback),


2. Exception flow ne message commit kiya.
Jab exception flow execute hota hai ya GUJ.NEFT.OUT.EXCEPTION_FLOW call hoti hai,
IIB automatically ek naya transaction context (Txn #2) start karta hai

